# The repo is authored on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but consumed on Linux —
# Vercel builds it and the profile-README GitHub Action renders it with headless
# Chromium. Pin text to LF everywhere so neither side sees a whole-file diff just
# because the other touched it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# run.bat is double-clicked by cmd.exe, which is happiest with CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.woff2 binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.webp  binary
*.rw2   binary

# The Projects Panel's recording, and the reason it is worth spelling out: until
# this repository carried a video these two extensions were governed by nothing
# but the `text=auto eol=lf` at the top, which would have run every CRLF-looking
# byte pair in a VP9 or H.264 stream through line-ending normalisation on a
# Windows checkout and produced a file no browser will decode.
#
# THEY ARE COMMITTED RAW, NEVER LFS. Vercel serves an LFS-tracked file as its
# pointer stub, so the clip would deploy as 130 bytes of text and the Panel would
# hold a black rectangle — a lesson already recorded against eater-map-site.
*.webm  binary
*.mp4   binary
